Monday
Today we ate lunch with Katayama san! Afterwards we went to a park and took
some pictures with him too. He actually requested some artwork, so I gave
it to him in person today, but a couple days later he sent me an email
asking me to change it =F0=9F=98=82 I guess that's what I get making an art=
 for
someone with such particular standards =F0=9F=A4=B7=E2=80=8D=E2=99=82=EF=B8=
=8F=F0=9F=98=81 After that we biked pretty
far to check out a secondhand store and the mall. At the mall there were
some people at a table and they were taking a survey of customers at the
mall the reward for taking the survey was a bag of potato chips so we
decided we'd stop by and take the survey because I love surveys LOL so we
sat down to take the survey they told us it would take just a few minutes
and we began and we noticed that it would take more than just a few minutes
LOL we ended up taking this survey for probably 10 minutes not
understanding most of it and we left with, as promised, a bag of chips. =F0=
=9F=98=82
The same night we also met at the church with Nishioka san and had a family
home evening activity as usual. We made some letters for friends and asked
Nishioka san to give one to one of her friends =F0=9F=98=81

Tuesday
Today we started off with a district meeting over Zoom, and had some great
housing too! We met a lady who was super sweet, and a guy who invited us
into his house to show us his ART AND ELECTRIC GUITAR????? You kidding Me?
We are absolutely Going back to jam out with bro. Today was also Eikaiwa,
and Matsuoka san brought me a late birthday present =F0=9F=91=80 It's a Suk=
imaswitch
CD 20th anniversary album!!!!!!!!!!! Literally the Album I listened to in
America that made me fall in love with Sukimaswitch. Thats an =E2=80=9Cup t=
here=E2=80=9D
birthday present =F0=9F=98=86

Wednesday
Played soccer with some kids at a park! One of them knows a kid who's going
to our activities, and he took some of our flyers to pass out to his
friends, and he's asking his mom to let him come to game night! We will see
how it goes!

Thursday
Today we met a few cool people housing, ome of which thought we were their
mother impersonating some young men =F0=9F=98=82 (through the doorbell voic=
ebox) as
well as had a fantastic Daytime Eikaiwa for the first time! 5 new people
showed up, and we already have an appointment set up with one of them!
=F0=9F=98=81=F0=9F=98=81=E2=9C=A8=EF=B8=8F A highlight for sure!

Friday
We met with Kimura san in his art store, and had a 2 way lesson about our
religions lol. Buddhism is really just all the beliefs of Christianity with
a different name attached to the deity which is pretty interesting and I
wouldn=E2=80=99t have expected. We also had Game night and attempted to vis=
it a
bunch of inactive members by bike (we weren't able to meet any of them =F0=
=9F=98=A2).
Solid day!

No more time to write so I'll talk about the rest next week!! I love you
